Let the cost of the bagel be $B$.
We are given that $B = $4$.
The soup cost 25% more than the bagel. So the cost of the soup is $S = B + 0.25B = 1.25B$.
Substituting $B = 4$, we get $S = 1.25 \times 4 = $5$.
The cake is half the price of the bagel. So the cost of the cake is $C = \frac{1}{2}B = \frac{1}{2} \times 4 = $2$.
The total cost for the dinner is $T = B + S + C = 4 + 5 + 2 = $11$.

